        // We'll simply call c.allowance(address(1), address(2)) - this triggers share call which goes to this contract's fallback.
        // This contract's fallback should try to call c.updatePrice(1) - which will succeed in buggy (auth modifier does nothing) and revert in reference (wards[msg.sender]==1 fails because msg.sender is this contract? Wait msg.sender in updatePrice context is this contract itself, which is authorized. Hmm.
